- **nscript** — ************************** nscript.flf ************************** nscript by Normand Veilleux <nveilleu@emr.ca> Oct 7, 1994 figletized by Peter Samuelson <psamuels@hmc.edu> Nov 29, 1994 Explanation of first line: flf2a - "magic number" for file identification =     - hardblank--like a blank, but won't smush 16    - height of a character 10    - height of a character, not including descenders 32    - max line length (after comments) -- currently in "W" 1     - default smushmode for this font 21    - number of comment lines Note: this font connects smoothly together, and to that end there are two sets of lowercase letters.  The "normal" set is where lowercase letters should be, and the "other" set, for use after lowercase b, o, v and w, replaces what I thought were the least essential characters in ASCII.  To use these, run your text through UNIX sed(1) with a long series of replace commands. ******************** and now, the font itself *******************
